  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="a268d9ef-92c2-407d-b3c2-d8626d953dfc" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="10c18699-63a8-4727-aef9-554b952c18ad" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=x^2+x\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2+x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-x^2+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2+3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the quadratic equation that represents each graph.</para>
      <para>
            <image alt="&lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 5, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 4 to 4, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 2 comma 2, 0 comma 0, and 2 comma 6.&lt;/p&gt;" height="171" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7dc411bbf2270de91b8434022d10d52c2ef5b03d" width="268"/></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=x^2+x\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b82293b7-d121-4b1a-af04-9a782684acca" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-x^2+2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2+x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-x^2+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2+3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>
            <image alt="&lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 5, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 4 to 4, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 1 comma 1, 0 comma 0, 2 comma 2.&lt;/p&gt;" height="171" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8c79633ee9db28ae376fd645f3305f7e040d6f37" width="268"/></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=-x^2+2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3904b634-9a02-4278-8669-0f52e59f3a73" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=x^2-x\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2+x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-x^2+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2+3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>
            <image alt="&lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 5, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 4 to 4, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 1 comma 1, 0 comma 0, 2 comma 2.&lt;/p&gt;" height="171" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7b2bcbdf48c57e9872e7e9cc5a2b0a45f04ff07e" width="268"/></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=x^2-x\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ac6c8d51-6ddd-408e-8c9a-09724b084945" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=x^2+3x\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2+x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-x^2+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2+3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>
            <image alt="&lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 5, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 4 to 4, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 3 comma 3, negative 1 comma negative 2, and 0 comma 0.&lt;/p&gt;" height="171" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2d6d2db94cfc98fa655c905ff086edd06b44a023" width="268"/></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=x^2+3x\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="47b221e5-5ecf-47ef-a87c-6397d45e81c0" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,0),(-12,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,0),(-12,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (3,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (16,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (-24,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Without graphing the equations, answer questions 2–5 to complete the table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Equation</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)-intercepts</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)-coordinate of vertex</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(y=x^2+12x\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>2a. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>2b. _____</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(y=x^2-3x\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>3a. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>3b. _____</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(y=-x^2+16x\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>4a. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>4b. _____</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(y=-x^2-24x\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>5a. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>5b. _____</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts and the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=x^2+12x\).</para>
      <para>
            <para> What are the \(x\)-intercepts for the equation \(y=x^2+12x\)?</para>
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((0,0),(-12,0)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.!</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3dcd0fb3-d5f6-4512-87e4-078c17bde828" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-6">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=x^2+12x\)? </para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -6</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="14d4938b-e405-400d-93d0-80c66d6d6c8f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,0), (3,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,0),(-12,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (3,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (16,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (-24,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts and the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=x^2-3x\).</para>
      <para>
            <para> What are the \(x\)-intercepts for the equation \(y=x^2-3x\)?</para>
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((0,0), (3,0)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7d788c97-8fc3-4ac2-9c93-5682536af420" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1.5">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=x^2-3x\)? </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! 1.5</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="44d02fe9-ead0-4214-a431-386e3bc84345" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,0), (16,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,0),(-12,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (3,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (16,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (-24,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts and the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=-x^2+16x\).</para>
      <para>
            <para> What are the \(x\)-intercepts for the equation \(y=-x^2+16x\)?</para>
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((0,0), (16,0)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c941cd33-a878-4346-989f-33be17d96f3b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="8">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=-x^2+16x\)? </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 8</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="daee3cea-92e3-4ed5-bfa5-8ec55ee29adb" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,0), (-24,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,0),(-12,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (3,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (16,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0), (-24,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts and the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=-x^2-24x\).</para>
      <para>
            <para> What are the \(x\)-intercepts for the equation \(y=-x^2-24x\)?</para>
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((0,0), (-24,0)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.3 and 7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f7b96024-18a1-40e0-9882-0fa5a72c36e2" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-12">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex for the equation \(y=-x^2-24x\)?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -12</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d6cf80d4-5580-4e13-8a35-00fd2bee55ae" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The graph would move to the right and down." data-solution-options="[&quot;The graph would move to the right and down.&quot;, &quot;The graph would move to the left and down.&quot;, &quot;The graph would move to the right and up.&quot;, &quot;The graph would move to the left and up.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here is a graph that represents \(y=x^2\).

          <image alt=" &lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 8 to 8, by 2’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 12 to 12, by 2’s. A curve, labeled y equals x squared, passes through the points negative 2 comma 4, 0 comma 0, and 2 comma 4.&lt;/p&gt;" height="172" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/24018f3ad80b39441a79406ca4974776c1d0d321" width="268"/> </para>
      <para>
          <para> Describe what would happen to the graph if the original equation were changed to \(y=x^2-6x\).</para>
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The graph would move to the right and down.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3ca7ea2c-96ba-4c27-973a-0a56c436cdc1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,0),(6,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,0),(6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0),(0,6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0),(-6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,0),(0,-6)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Predict the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph if the original equation were changed to \(y=x^2-6x\).</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((0,0),(6,0)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="430d5ce7-c22e-4d78-bbf5-ec84afbfdc46" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Fourth" data-solution-options="[&quot;First&quot;, &quot;Second&quot;, &quot;Third&quot;, &quot;Fourth&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>In which quadrant is the vertex located if the original equation were changed to \(y=x^2-6x\)?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Fourth Quadrant</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="acf83bce-9750-4918-a6ff-1dcc561f61ac" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(y=(2x−1)^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2−8x−7\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-x^2+9x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=10x−5x^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=(2x−1)^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=(1−x)(2+x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2−8x−7\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para><emphasis>Select two </emphasis>equations whose graph opens upward.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=(2x−1)^2\), \(y=x^2−8x−7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0e291e11-6eef-42fb-9eeb-31e8067d7732" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Graph A" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Technology required. Use the three graphs to answer questions a–c. Then, use graphing technology to check each equation.</para>
      <para>Graph A</para>
      <image alt="&quot;Parabola. Opens up. X intercepts = 0&amp;nbsp;and -7.&amp;nbsp;&quot;" height="211" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4aeafc491ae29b91a96c11b8e424555b36123a02" width="267"/><para>Graph B</para>
      <image alt="&quot;Parabola. Opens up. Vertex = 0&amp;nbsp;comma -16.&amp;nbsp;X intercepts = -4 and 4.&amp;nbsp;&quot;" height="215" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1b3fec958046c05f54fe8dfa7e6bd83312caad5b" width="264"/><para>Graph C</para>
      <image alt="&quot;Parabola. Opens up. X intercepts = -9&amp;nbsp;and 3.&amp;nbsp;&quot;" height="216" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7543018bfe177a32a2e0ddd1ecea70ee4bae2dc3" width="270"/><para>Which graph represents the equation \(f(x)=x(x+7)\) or \(f(x)=x^2+7x\)? Then, use graphing technology to check your answer. </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Graph A </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ed2a78ec-d3d7-400c-bbf2-5f40578b5460" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Graph B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph represents the equation \(g(x)=(x+4)(x−4)\) or \(g(x)=x^2−16\)? Then, use graphing technology to check your answer. </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Graph B </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="437286ec-77dc-4d6c-a768-4e4ee1a8bd6a" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Graph C" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph represents the equation \(h(x)=(x−3)(x+9)\) or \(h(x)=x^2+6x−27\)? Then, use graphing technology to check your answer. </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Graph C</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.13.2–7.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
